Also install the generated .proto/.proto3 files alongside the headers.

onnxruntime's vcpkg build consumes onnx as a pure package dependency (it never
builds onnx's sources itself), but onnxruntime_proto.cmake still needs
onnx/onnx-ml.proto / onnx-operators-ml.proto at configure time to regenerate
its own protobuf bindings against the same schema. Upstream only installs the
generated headers, not the .proto files they were generated from.

Rebased onto onnx v1.22.0 from vcpkg's ports/onnx/fix-cmakelists.patch
(vcpkg registry, synced 2025-12-27); only the line numbers moved, the
onnxruntime_INSTALL guard around the install() calls is new since then.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 8b5af30..6836651 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -600,6 +600,10 @@ if(ONNX_INSTALL)
           DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
           FILES_MATCHING
           PATTERN "*.h")
+  install(DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/onnx DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
+          FILES_MATCHING PATTERN "*.proto")
+  install(DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/onnx DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}
+          FILES_MATCHING PATTERN "*.proto3")
 endif()

 configure_file(
